{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-350410",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The Hadamard product of two compatible vectors $u$ and $v$ can be expressed as the matrix product\n\n$$\nv⊙u=\\text{diag}(v)u.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nBy=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(AB)\\cdot (By) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\text{diag}([\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]⊙[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
